L121: 4 RELATIVISTICS
L122: Mathematical aspects of relativistics, i.e., relativity theory, and mathematical methods associated with that theory. Papers dealing with specific applications to fields and physics are collected in Chaps. 5 and 6.
L123: The exception to this rule is Sec. 4.6 on general relativity theory which does not allow for such a separation since according to it gravitation is a purely geometrical effect.
L124: 4.1 SPECIAL-RELATIVITY
L125: Lorentz transformations and representations of the Lorentz group (rotations, boosts, and improper transformations), as well as more general rotations in Minkowskian or Euclidian four-space, including discrete transformations.
L126: See also ELECTRODYNAMICS, Sec. 6.4, in particular for the seminal papers of A.W. Conway and L. Silberstein.
