L146: 4.5 TWISTOR
L147: Twistors may be regarded as spinors of the O(4, 2) group, which is two-to-one isomorphic with the full 15-parameter conformal group in Minkowski space, including the full Poincaré group. As 8-dimensional points in complexified space-time, twistors are able to encode angular-momentum/spin in addition to position/translation. They were introduced by Roger Penrose as possibly more fundamental physical objects than 4-dimensional points in Minkowski space-time.
L148: 1. R. Penrose, Twistor algebra, J. Math. Phys. 8 (1967) 345–366. 2. R. Penrose, Twistor quantization and curved space-time, Int. J. Theor. Phys. 1 (1968) 61–99.
