L292: 8.4 EDDINGTON (“Eddington numbers”)
L293: The “E-numbers” introduced by Arthur S. Eddington in 1928 are equivalent to elements of the algebra of the Dirac matrices, i.e., to elements of the Clifford algebra Cl_{4,1}. Eddington’s formalism corresponds to the first use of Clifford numbers in relation to Dirac’s theory.
