L295: 8.5 SEMIVECTOR (“Einstein-Mayer’s spinors”)
L296: Semivectors were introduced in 1932 by Einstein and his assistant Walter Mayer, possibly in reaction to the work on Dirac’s equation by his previous assistant, Cornelius Lanczos. Einstein-Mayer’s formulation of Dirac’s equation is based on 4 \times 4 matrices which in flat spacetime reduces to Lanczos’s biquaternionic formulation.
